$DIR/main.p:30:6: q holds a view of b (&b, line 27), which was moved into take2 (its parameter takes a Buf by value) at line 29, so q can no longer be used here
    q looks at memory that b owns, without owning it: the view was made by &b at
    line 27. A view of an owner held in a local variable may be used only while
    the variable keeps the value the view was made from. At line 29 b was moved
    into take2 (its parameter takes a Buf by value), so the view may look at
    memory that was released, or at a value that now belongs to something else.
    Go keeps memory alive for as long as any pointer refers to it. Plutonium has
    no garbage collector: an owner releases its memory when it is dropped, so a
    view must not be used after the value it looks at has gone.
    Use q before line 29, or move b only after the last use of q
    Or move a copy at line 29, so that b keeps its value:
        b.Clone()
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3313" for a longer explanation)
